From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Probe HTTP HLS segments without filename checks.

After the legacy user-agent retry succeeds, the local VRChat issue #748
reproduction still fails in FFmpeg's HLS test_segment(), before downloading
any media. The playlist serves MPEG-TS segments with .js, .css, .woff and
other non-media suffixes. FFmpeg rejects these with AVERROR_INVALIDDATA.
The same source opens as H.264/AAC and decodes successfully with content
probing instead of segment filename validation.

Disable extension_picky for HTTP(S) inputs, including playlists detected
by content rather than by the URL. Setting allowed_segment_extensions to
ALL alone would still fail the later demuxer-to-extension comparison.

Explicitly restrict these inputs to HTTP's network protocols and inline
data. Local-file, subfile, concat and pipe access remain forbidden even
when extension checks are disabled. Leave the local-file extension allow
list and all RTSP/local input handling unchanged.

Issue: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/748

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_demuxer.c
@@ -884,6 +884,13 @@ NTSTATUS demuxer_create( void *arg )
             /* FFmpeg accepts rtsp:// plus an explicit transport option. */
             memmove( url + 4, url + 5, strlen( url + 5 ) + 1 );
         }
+        if (!rtsp)
+        {
+            /* HTTP HLS segments need not have media filename extensions. Probe
+             * their contents, but never allow remote playlists to open local files. */
+            av_dict_set( &options, "protocol_whitelist", "http,https,tls,rtp,tcp,udp,crypto,httpproxy,data", 0 );
+            av_dict_set( &options, "extension_picky", "0", 0 );
+        }
         if (rtsp) av_dict_set( &options, "timeout", "15000000", 0 );
         else if (!hls) av_dict_set( &options, "rw_timeout", "15000000", 0 );
         if (progressive)
